{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1012 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "1b06de783787a8deab02fa22445d4c64d557b0843b92d6e5ebcfd08445008484" :edb/db-before-t 1011 :edb/db-after-t 1012 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534324 50 #inst "2026-10-11T19:11:21.988Z" 13194139534324 17592186045417 true] [17592186172054 1038 #edb/ref 17592186419017 13194139534324 17592186045417 true] [17592186419011 1080 "I and II only" 13194139534324 17592186045417 true] [17592186419011 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534324 17592186045417 true] [17592186419011 1083 #uuid "6d16442d-19e4-582c-8e49-f56bc5ac7989" 13194139534324 17592186045417 true] [17592186419012 1080 "II, III and IV only" 13194139534324 17592186045417 true] [17592186419012 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534324 17592186045417 true] [17592186419012 1083 #uuid "8c4765c6-63f6-569c-bd76-1517cf62b38c" 13194139534324 17592186045417 true] [17592186419013 1080 "II only" 13194139534324 17592186045417 true] [17592186419013 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534324 17592186045417 true] [17592186419013 1083 #uuid "91c67dbf-ae46-5cea-83af-1664e56a1941" 13194139534324 17592186045417 true] [17592186419014 1080 "I only" 13194139534324 17592186045417 true] [17592186419014 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534324 17592186045417 true] [17592186419014 1083 #uuid "eb70dc47-8da4-592d-92b1-cbf8738afc59" 13194139534324 17592186045417 true] [17592186419015 1080 "I and III only" 13194139534324 17592186045417 true] [17592186419015 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534324 17592186045417 true] [17592186419015 1083 #uuid "fea9db8f-ed00-5f80-923f-1ea3dcb8fe89" 13194139534324 17592186045417 true] [17592186419016 1075 #edb/ref 17592186419011 13194139534324 17592186045417 true] [17592186419016 1075 #edb/ref 17592186419012 13194139534324 17592186045417 true] [17592186419016 1075 #edb/ref 17592186419013 13194139534324 17592186045417 true] [17592186419016 1075 #edb/ref 17592186419014 13194139534324 17592186045417 true] [17592186419016 1075 #edb/ref 17592186419015 13194139534324 17592186045417 true] [17592186419016 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534324 17592186045417 true] [17592186419016 1077 "selection" 13194139534324 17592186045417 true] [17592186419016 1078 #edb/ref 17592186419011 13194139534324 17592186045417 true] [17592186419016 1079 #uuid "e6809d48-fda2-518b-8b59-a579c69de413" 13194139534324 17592186045417 true] [17592186419017 1068 #edb/ref 17592186419016 13194139534324 17592186045417 true] [17592186419017 1069 "q-125796" 13194139534324 17592186045417 true] [17592186419017 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534324 17592186045417 true] [17592186419017 1071 "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=⟨-y,\\,x⟩$ and the points $A(0,1)$ and $B(0,-1)$ in the $xy$-plane. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\ne 0,$ where ${C}_{1}$ is the path along the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1,$ traversed from $A$ to $B$ in counterclockwise direction.\n- ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0,$ where ${C}_{2}$ is the path along the segment line $\\overset{―}{AB},$ traversed from $A$ to $B.$\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ is independent of path.\n- $F$ is conservative." 13194139534324 17592186045417 true] [17592186419017 1072 #uuid "b47df0de-b5ee-5562-b36a-a659cbe48d85" 13194139534324 17592186045417 true] [17592186419017 1074 "Let $C$ be a piecewise-smooth curve given by the vector-valued function $r(t)$ for $t\\in [a,b].$ Let $f$ be a differentiable function of two or three variables such that $∇f$ is continuous on $C.$ The fundamental theorem for line integrals states that \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=f(r(b))-f(r(a)).\n$$\n\n \n\nThis theorem implies that the line integral of a conservative vector field depends only on the value of $f$ at the initial and terminal points $A$ and $B,$ and is independent of the path between them.\n\nWith that in mind, we consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Parameterizing the curve, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{1}(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,t\\in [\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{3\\pi }{2}].\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\cdot ⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}1\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =t{|}_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =\\pi  \\\\  & \\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Parameterizing the line segment, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{2}(t)=⟨0,\\,1-2t⟩,\\,t\\in [0,1].\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}⟨2t-1,\\,0⟩\\cdot ⟨0,\\,-2⟩\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}0\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ have the same initial and terminal points, yet\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\ne {\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,\n$$\n\nwe conclude that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ is path-dependent.\n\n- Statement IV is false. If a vector field is conservative then it is path-independent. Since $F$ is path-dependent, it is not conservative." 13194139534324 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-6d16442d-19e4-582c-8e49-f56bc5ac7989" 17592186419011 "answer-8c4765c6-63f6-569c-bd76-1517cf62b38c" 17592186419012 "answer-91c67dbf-ae46-5cea-83af-1664e56a1941" 17592186419013 "answer-eb70dc47-8da4-592d-92b1-cbf8738afc59" 17592186419014 "answer-fea9db8f-ed00-5f80-923f-1ea3dcb8fe89" 17592186419015 "answer-field-e6809d48-fda2-518b-8b59-a579c69de413" 17592186419016 "question-b47df0de-b5ee-5562-b36a-a659cbe48d85" 17592186419017}}
